                "Under Quadratic Voting, the cost of casting V votes on a specific proposal is proportional to the square of those votes: Cost(V) = V^2. Equivalently, if a community member possesses C voting credits or governance tokens, the number of votes they can cast is the square root of their allocated tokens: V = sqrt(C). This mathematical formulation fundamentally rebalances voting influence: casting 1 vote costs 1 credit, casting 2 votes costs 4 credits, casting 3 votes costs 9 credits, casting 10 votes costs 100 credits, and casting 100 votes costs 10,000 credits. Consequently, an individual with 10,000 tokens can cast 100 votes, whereas one hundred passionate individual consumers each holding 100 tokens can cast 10 votes each, yielding a collective total of 1,000 votes. Quadratic Voting thus mathematically amplifies the collective voice of a broad, passionate community over the concentrated wealth of a single individual.",
